high winds and low humidity are  hampering firefighters trying to control  a 300 acre wildfire near the town of  leones in northern colorado the smoke  and flames forced dozens of evacuations  friday there are no reported injuries  the cause of the fire has not been  determined and about 185  miles south of albuquerque new mexico  donations in food and clothing of food  and clothing are pouring in to help  wildfire victims the fire is blamed for  at least two deaths while burning up  more than 240 homes and more than 6  thousand acres
 

